1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:02,040
One campaign.

2
00:00:02,090 --> 00:00:04,450
A hundred and twenty-three readers.

3
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:06,990
Three hundred and sixty-nine choices.

4
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:09,460
Could you say why each one was made?

5
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:18,180
Most companies end up
choosing between two things.

6
00:00:18,230 --> 00:00:21,230
A tool that's easy, until they outgrow it.

7
00:00:21,280 --> 00:00:26,390
And a system that's powerful, until
they try to change it, or leave it.

8
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:35,720
But AI has changed what a company,
or its agency, can build for itself.

9
00:00:35,770 --> 00:00:40,600
So what if it kept the core, its
content, its campaigns, its rules,

10
00:00:40,650 --> 00:00:45,550
its consent, and everything around
it were a part you could replace?

11
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:54,180
A CRM, a shop, a warehouse,
an analytics tool:

12
00:00:54,230 --> 00:00:57,740
other systems reach the
core through the API,

13
00:00:57,790 --> 00:01:01,370
each with its own key
and its own permissions.

14
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:09,720
This is a reference for building a
communication system you control.

15
00:01:14,600 --> 00:01:16,800
A manager starts with content.

16
00:01:16,850 --> 00:01:21,520
Written once, kept in one place,
and scored by what it's about.

17
00:01:22,600 --> 00:01:25,910
A campaign doesn't copy
it; it points to it.

18
00:01:25,960 --> 00:01:30,260
When one headline has to
change, only that email changes.

19
00:01:32,600 --> 00:01:35,410
Now one email with a slot in the middle.

20
00:01:35,460 --> 00:01:40,190
The slot picks for each reader,
from content a person marked ready.

21
00:01:40,240 --> 00:01:43,690
Same email, three readers,
three different picks.

22
00:01:43,740 --> 00:01:45,970
And every pick can be explained.

23
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:54,840
AI can suggest and draft.

24
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:02,130
A person decides what goes out.

25
00:02:08,300 --> 00:02:12,430
Even when a machine asks to
send, someone has to say yes.

26
00:02:14,600 --> 00:02:17,870
Before anything leaves,
the system plans the send,

27
00:02:17,920 --> 00:02:22,310
shows how many people it can reach,
and freezes what they will get.

28
00:02:24,600 --> 00:02:27,420
Afterwards, open any reader's message:

29
00:02:27,470 --> 00:02:32,260
the content they received, and
the reason each piece was picked.

30
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:40,210
Their clicks come back as
signals that fade with time,

31
00:02:40,260 --> 00:02:41,840
and shape the next pick.

32
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:48,230
Behind the screens, a
developer keeps it growing,

33
00:02:48,280 --> 00:02:50,640
by hand or with an AI assistant.

34
00:02:50,690 --> 00:02:54,020
Not by asking a vendor,
but by adding a file.

35
00:02:56,600 --> 00:02:58,070
A new content block:

36
00:02:58,120 --> 00:03:00,040
a manifest and a template.

37
00:03:00,090 --> 00:03:01,940
It appears in the editor.

38
00:03:08,600 --> 00:03:11,060
A new way to decide who sees what:

39
00:03:11,110 --> 00:03:14,310
one file, written by
whoever knows the data.

40
00:03:20,600 --> 00:03:21,540
A new AI task.

41
00:03:21,590 --> 00:03:28,580
The developer defines what it may read and return;
the wording of the prompt belongs to the manager.

42
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:36,660
Even the delivery provider
is a part, not a foundation.

43
00:03:36,710 --> 00:03:39,270
Email or push, any sending service:

44
00:03:39,320 --> 00:03:43,600
a file and a few lines, and
the company changes who sends,

45
00:03:43,650 --> 00:03:45,690
without touching a campaign.

46
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:50,580
The reason stays with the code.

47
00:03:50,630 --> 00:03:53,260
Files point to the decisions behind them,

48
00:03:53,310 --> 00:03:57,700
including the rules for working with
AI, all in the same repository.

49
00:04:00,600 --> 00:04:01,450
One campaign:

50
00:04:01,500 --> 00:04:05,480
an email for some readers, a
push notification for others,

51
00:04:05,530 --> 00:04:07,420
each shaped for its channel.

52
00:04:12,300 --> 00:04:13,040
Audiences.

53
00:04:13,090 --> 00:04:13,600
Brands.

54
00:04:13,650 --> 00:04:14,080
Roles.

55
00:04:14,130 --> 00:04:14,710
Consent.

56
00:04:14,760 --> 00:04:16,700
A record of who did what.

57
00:04:16,750 --> 00:04:19,400
All in one place, all of it yours.

58
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:23,370
See what it does.

59
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:25,260
Change it with a file.

60
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:27,200
Keep the core.

61
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:31,590
Building a communication
system you control.

62
00:04:31,640 --> 00:04:33,720
Always adapting to your business.
